<source id="1" url="https://chat.codercops.com/core/tools/" title="Tools" section="Built-in: Lead Capture">
Tools > Built-in: Lead Capture

The `LeadCaptureTool` lets the AI collect contact information from conversations:

```typescript
import { LeadCaptureTool } from '@chatcops/core';

const leadTool = new LeadCaptureTool(async (lead) => {
  console.log('New lead:', lead);
  // Save to database, CRM, send webhook, etc.
});
```
</source>
<source id="2" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/express/" title="Express Adapter" section="With Lead Capture">
Express Adapter > With Lead Capture

```typescript
import { LeadCaptureTool } from '@chatcops/core';
import express from 'express';
import { chatcopsMiddleware } from '@chatcops/server';

const app = express();
const db = { leads: { create: async (_lead: unknown) => {} } };

app.all('/chat', chatcopsMiddleware({
  provider: {
    type: 'claude',
    apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY!,
  },
  systemPrompt: 'You are a helpful assistant. Capture leads when users share contact info.',
  tools: [
    new LeadCaptureTool(async (lead) => {
      // Save to your database, CRM, etc.
      await db.leads.create(lead);
      console.log('Lead captured:', lead.email);
    }),
  ],
}));
```
</source>
<source id="3" url="https://chat.codercops.com/core/tools/" title="Tools">
Tools

Tools extend the AI's capabilities by letting it perform actions like capturing leads, querying databases, or calling APIs.
</source>
<source id="4" url="https://chat.codercops.com/server/vercel/" title="Vercel Adapter" section="Full Example with Tools">
Vercel Adapter > Full Example with Tools

```typescript
import { chatcopsVercelHandler } from '@chatcops/server';
import { LeadCaptureTool, FAQKnowledgeSource } from '@chatcops/core';

export const config = { runtime: 'edge' };

export default chatcopsVercelHandler({
  provider: {
    type: 'claude',
    apiKey: process.env.ANTHROPIC_API_KEY!,
    model: 'claude-haiku-5-5',
  },
  systemPrompt: `You are the AI assistant for Acme Corp.
    Help users with product questions and capture leads.`,
  tools: [
    new LeadCaptureTool(async (lead) => {
      await fetch('https://hooks.zapier.com/...', {
        method: 'POST',
        body: JSON.stringify(lead),
      });
    }),
  ],
  knowledge: [
    new FAQKnowledgeSource([
      { question: 'Pricing?', answer: 'Plans start at $29/mo.' },
    ]),
  ],
  allowedOrigins: ['*'],
});
```
</source>
<source id="5" url="https://chat.codercops.com/core/analytics/" title="Analytics" section="AnalyticsCollector API">
Analytics > AnalyticsCollector API

```typescript
import { AnalyticsCollector } from '@chatcops/core';

const analytics = new AnalyticsCollector();

// Track custom events
analytics.track('pricing.viewed', { plan: 'Team' });

// Get aggregated stats
const stats = analytics.getStats();
// {
//   totalConversations: 150,
//   totalMessages: 2340,
//   leadsCaptured: 23,
//   averageMessagesPerConversation: 15.6,
//   eventCounts: { 'conversation.started': 150, ... }
// }

// Get raw events (optionally filter by type)
const allEvents = analytics.getEvents();
const leads = analytics.getEvents('lead.captured');

// Clear all events
analytics.clear();
```
</source>
</sources>

